Winged rubber dam retainer in endodontics is a device used to isolate the tooth during dental procedures. It has several advantages, including providing a stable field, allowing for better visualization of the canal system, and enabling extra bucco-lingual retraction of the gingiva. It also allows the placement of dam, clamp, and frame in one operation.

