The primary site of action of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) is on the distal tubules and collecting ducts in the kidney. These structures are responsible for concentrating urine by reabsorbing water back into the bloodstream. ADH does this by increasing the permeability of these tubules to water, which reduces the volume of urine produced.

