The most frequently recommended tooth brushing technique for periodontal patients is the sulcular technique. This technique focuses on cleaning the sulcus (the space between the tooth and the gingiva), which is crucial for removing plaque and preventing periodontal disease. It is considered the gold standard for effective plaque removal in periodontal care.

The scrub technique involves aggressive brushing and is not typically recommended for periodontal patients due to the risk of damaging the gingiva. The roll technique is less effective for cleaning the sulcus. The Fones technique is not a standard or recognized brushing technique in periodontal care.

